      "writtenOn": "2022-10-07T21:41:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are 2 reasons we can\u0027t use `std::packaged_task`:\n\n1. MSVC\u0027s implementation of `std::packaged_task` is buggy, so we can\u0027t use move only `Item` type with MSVC\u0027s `std::packaged_task`. See https://developercommunity.visualstudio.com/t/unable-to-move-stdpackaged-task-into-any-stl-conta/108672. And we are using `WorkerThread` to dispatch move only `Item`. There is a workaround for this: we can always ask the caller to wrap the `Item` in a `std::shared_ptr` so that `Item` is always copyable. WDYT?\n\n2. We need the ability to set the returned `std::future` to be ready without having to process the `Item`, so that on exit, the caller won\u0027t end up with future that won\u0027t be ready forever. I am not sure how that could be achieved with `std::packaged_task`. We can share the reference to `mFinished` and let the functor passed to `std::packaged_task` to always test if `mFinished` is set and return early, but it seems that we are reinventing `std::promise` by using `std::packaged_task`.",
      "parentUuid": "d6a4a0e0_fc2048cb",
      "revId": "293cd774c4960df66e8ea3743f9e6e7101130981",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
