      "writtenOn": "2022-10-10T17:27:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think the code currently does what you intend, though.\n\nExample:\n\n1. mFinished is set to true by some other thread after it\u0027s checked on line 120\n2. We enqueue a new task and signal the worker thread\n3. The worker thread gets the task from the queue and starts processing it (line 147)\n4. The task is processed as a normal work item. `shouldStop` is false at that point so we won\u0027t go into the `shouldStop` branch.\n\nOne way to fix would be to add `if(mFinished) return;` after we wake up from waiting (e.g. on line 144)",
      "parentUuid": "ad663f1e_17169ba8",
      "revId": "293cd774c4960df66e8ea3743f9e6e7101130981",
