      },
      "lineNbr": 144,
      "author": {
        "id": 1576895
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-07T21:41:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we need to do the refactor and I believe you overlook the potential performance cost.\n\n* For readability and maintainability: if we replace the swap to `std::vector` with popping and process the `Command` one by one, the only extra 2 lines we get rid of are the declaration of `todo` and the following `for` loop. Besides, chromium\u0027s class `DelayedTaskManager` with a similar function is using the same pattern: https://crsrc.org/c/base/task/thread_pool/delayed_task_manager.cc;l\u003d124, so I would assume this degree of complexity won\u0027t hurt maintainability badly.\n\n* Note that `mQueue` is a `std::vector`, so the extra cost to remove the first item from the `std::vector` is O(n). Therefore, the proposed solution doesn\u0027t only increases the time we try to lock and wait for the conditional variable, we need also to pay extra time in removing the item. I agree this can be solved by changing `mQueue` to a `std::list`.\n\nWDYT?",
